A||||3||wkayl||Happy days...||||6||
Z||000000||wkayl||02-08-2001||12:41 AM||||My 86GT had an exhaust leak on the "front" manifold.  After 2 evenings (not working very hard so it took 2) I twisted off only 1 bolt on the "Y" pipe and pinched only 1 finger.  Boy that top A/C bolt was a ....well you get the idea.  When I got ready to remove the manifold I found the 2 manifold bolts behind the A/C finger tight.  I did remove the manifold as to replace the gasket, but have no cracks in the pipe.  I already removed the broken bolt and ready to get gaskets to start putting it back together.  Thank goodness for a heated garage for we have freezing rain tonight with snow for tomorrow.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/outline.jpg">   <BR>86GT original paint, interior, engine  <A HREF="http://www.fierowayne.homestead.com/fierowayne.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fierowayne.homestead.com/fierowayne.html</A> ||||reg||6
Z||000001||FieroJoe||02-08-2001||10:17 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>I twisted off only 1 bolt on the "Y" pipe and pinched only 1 finger.<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>For an exhaust job, that dosent sound too bad!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Voytek||02-08-2001||02:24 PM||||Hey<BR>I'm currently removing both of my manifolds and installing Sprint manifolds from FS.  The rear one is out and the front one is most of the way there.  Except - that damn bolt behind the AC compressor!  What year is your car and how did you get it out w/o removing the compressor?||||reg||1
Z||000003||wkayl||02-08-2001||02:56 PM||||86 GT.  I had to remove the A/C compressor.  The top bold to the clutch end of the compressor was tough.  I removed the rear compressor bracket from the compressor and let it hang on the A/C lines and use a swivel socket even though it didn't fit too good.  It will be interesting putting it back on.||||reg||1
